p.com/hike-to-eat/events/316535271/","description":"The Bridle Path is famous for being the richest address in Toronto. Most people don't realize that the neighbourhood just to the north is equally affluent. Fife Road and Fifeshire Road are lined with swanky mansions, one of which was featured in a highly successful Canadian comedy.\n\nThis hike is an opportunity to gawk at luxury homes before we exit into the lush foliage of Windfields Park. The park is also home to the bucolic Canadian Film Centre.\n\nUnfortunately, rich neighbourhoods don't have good restaurants. There's only one decent one, a Cantonese restaurant, where we can have dinner.\n\n**Highlights**\n\n1. York Mills Arena (depart 6:15 pm)\n2. Mansions of Fifeshire Rd\n3. St. Andrews Park\n4. York Mills and Bayview Ave (depart 6:55 pm)\n5. Canadian Film Centre\n6. Windfields Park\n7. Banbury Community Centre (depart 7:30 pm)\n8. Pearl Chinese Cuisine (arrive 7:55 pm)\n\n**Neighbourhoods**\nSt Andrews > Windfields\n\n**Map**\n[https://www.google.com/maps/d/edit?mid=1LX-fTnFET4MwGjl5zzE6CG1epvLdcTM&usp=sharing](https://www.google.com/maps/d/edit?mid=1LX-fTnFET4MwGjl5zzE6CG1epvLdcTM&usp=sharing)\n\n**How it works**\nHike starts punctually. Late or can't do the whole route? Meet us at scheduled checkpoints.\n\nSee our [home page](https://www.meetup.com/hike-to-eat/) for more info.","startDate":"2026-10-06T22:15:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"York Mills Arena","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"2539 Bayview Ave, North York, ON M2L 2Y4, Canada, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Hike to Eat","url":"https://www.meetup.com/hike-to-eat/"},"performer":"Hike to Eat"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Silent Bookclub Meeting #95","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-silent-book-club-meetup-group/events/316788804/","description":"The next event is happening on Tuesday October 6 at 6:00 PM at the Deck located in Clarence Square!\n\nPlease RSVP if you're planning on coming so we can plan appropriately!\n\nTo help cover the costs of meetup fees, we will be taking optional donations for this event. If you're inclined to, feel free to send any amount you're comfortable with to harresh.s@hotmail.com, or bring cash to the event. Please note that this is entirely optional and not required to join the event! All proceeds will go towards fees for this event and future events, as well as meetup fees","startDate":"2026-10-06T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Clarence Square Off Leash Dog Park","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"25 Clarence Square - King St W/Spadina Ave, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Silent Book Club (Toronto)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-silent-book-club-meetup-group/"},"performer":"Silent Book Club (Toronto)"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Trivia Night @Stout Irish Pub - Tuesday October 6th, 2026 at 6:45 PM","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-over-50-meetup-group/events/316455378/","description":"Let's get together for trivia and toasting, while tasting some delicious food!\nCome join us for an exciting Trivia Night on **Tuesday**, October 6th, 2026 at **6:45 AM (sharp)** at Stout Irish Pub, The venue is known for it's authentic Irish pub experience and hospitality. A fun and interactive night with great food, attentive staff and general trivia. There is a **minimum** **$10 per person** spend on food / drinks. Click [here](https://www.stoutirishpub.ca/menu) for a link to the food menu and [here](https://www.stoutirishpub.ca/drink-menu) for a link to the drink menu. Meet friends and make some new ones while enjoying a great night out! Each participant will cover their own food and drink costs. **The venue requests to please arrive on time.**\n**There is a non-refundable / non-transferable $5.00 cover fee** to attend this group event. This charge will reserve your spot, help with group costs and hopefully minimize no shows. **Payment of the $5 cover charge is due by TUESDAY, SEPTEMBER 29th, 2026.** After this date, non payment of the cover fee will result in the Member's name being moved to the \"not going\" list so that those \"waitlisted\" have an opportunity to attend the event.\nIn consideration of others, if you are not able to attend, please advise 48 hours prior to the event to allow other people on the waitlist to have your spot. No shows and less than 48 hours notice of non-attendance will be noted. 2 or more such occurrences will unfortunately lead to removal from the group. Thank you all for your understanding and consideration.\nHere are the details for the $5.00 e-transfer - E-mail - [weekendbrunchover50@hotmail.com](http://weekendbrunchover50@hotmail.com/), Security Question - What is the the event? **trivia**\nHope to see you there!","startDate":"2026-10-06T22:45:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Stout Irish pub","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"CA","streetAddress":"221 Carlton St., Toronto, ON M5A 2L2, Canada,, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Weekend Brunch and More for Ladies Over 50 (Ladies Only)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-over-50-meetup-group/"},"performer":"Weekend Brunch and More for Ladies Over 50 (Ladies Only)"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Pickering - Practical Philosophy Meetup 🇨🇦","url":"https://www.meetup.com/practical-philosophy-club-ontario/events/316588098/","description":"**🏛️ WHAT'S PRACTICAL PHILOSOPHY ABOUT?**\n\nPractical Philosophy is a weekly meet-up that brings critical thinkers together for an opportunity to dive deep on a topic, practice communicating, and building a community. All with no ‘official’ philosophy knowledge required! 😎\n\nPractical Philosophy is based on the idea that philosophy should be accessible to all, and not something reserved only for academics. Each week we choose a topic, and the goal is to use the conversation to develop our critical thinking and communication as we explore that topic.\nThe goal is to help develop our Critical Thinking, Communication, and Community 🙌\n\n**📓 HOW DOES IT WORK?**\n\nEach week, we pick one topic and discuss it. The topic for the week is shared, generally in the [Whatsapp group](https://tally.so/r/WORMLP), along with jump-off points to get the conversation going.\n\nWhen groups get bigger than 7-8 people, it’s important that we break into smaller groups. This way we are able to maintain a conversational flow as opposed to having our meetups feel like a discourse or lecture.\n\n**General Meeting Agenda**\nEach Practical Philosophy meet-up follows this general timeline:\n\n* 19:00-19:15 - People arrive and chat, get to know each other before the official start.\n* 19:15-19:25 - Meeting introduction, explanation of Practical Philosophy and the topic for the week, read the guidelines and the overview so attendees know what to expect in terms of timelines.\n* 19:25-20:45 - Break into small groups - introduce yourselves and general thoughts on the topic, open discussion afterwards. At this point the group can review the ‘jump-off’ questions as needed, but they are just there to help guide the conversation. It’s not obligatory to answer them.\n* 20:45-21:00 - Bring everyone back together to discuss conclusions of the topic - each group gives a short 1-minute summary. Organizer concludes the meeting and everyone takes a group photo.\n* 21:00 - The official meeting is over but it’s a great opportunity to get to know people in a non-structured environment, so we often stick around, chat, and get to know each other.\n\n**🧧PRICING?**\n\nPractical Philosophy is operated entirely on voluntary donations! If we are meeting in a café, buy a beverage! Donations are 100% voluntary, but they help us to bring the gift of deep conversation to people around the world. If you'd like to support, you can [donate here](https://www.zeffy.com/en-CA/donation-form/donate-to-practical-philosophy)!\n(Practical Philosophy is a registered Canadian charity)\n\n**💛 WHAT PEOPLE SAY ABOUT PRACTICAL PHILOSOPHY**\n\n**🗣** “I feel like Philosophy Club helps someone build their own belief system through a series of perspectives while not promoting what’s right and wrong” - Ekam\n\n🗣 “I got hooked from day 1 (the topic was authority) and felt it was the right place for me. I feel it is a place where people can go to learn and discuss new perspectives and increase critical thinking and community by interacting with people who might challenge your point of views but at the same time encourage you to have openness and mind flexibility.” - Daniel\n\n**🤓 FAQ**\n\n* **Do I need to study or read anything to attend?**\n\nNo preparation is necessary. This isn’t a study of other thinkers. We want to know what you think about the topic, not what an old philosopher thought. If you have a perspective from a religion or a school of thought to share, throw it on the table and we’ll discuss it.\n\n* **Is there a specific philosophy that Practical Philosophy is focused on?**\n\nThe goal of our meet-ups is to not have dogmatic discussions, and flex our critical thinking muscles. Because of this, we want to hear from every realm of thought, and don't study a particular school.\n\n* **Is it mostly men that attend?**\n\nSurprisingly, no! Although often, philosophy is seen as a Candelabra affair in a dark room with a bunch of guys, our Practical Philosophy meetups are generally 50/50 between genders, and we don’t meet in any dark rooms.\n\n* **Can I come alone?**\n\nOf course you can, we encourage it :)\n\n* **Can I be late?**\n\nPlease don't be! We do have a 15 minute grace period where we allow people to funnel in while we hang out, but after that if you arrive too late, it disrupts the flow of the conversation.\n\n* **Where do you meet?**\n\nThe location is posted in Meetup and our [Whatsapp](https://tally.so/r/WORMLP) group for this location. It is HIGHLY RECOMMENDED that you join the Whatsapp group! If you want to know what other cities have a Practical Philosophy Club, you can see our chapters on our [website](https://www.practicalphilosophy.club/).\n\n🤝**POLICY**\n\nTo respect our members privacy, we ask that no one privately message a member without first getting explicit consent. (This looks like speaking in person and being asked to message privately.) Contacting or texting other participants without prior consent is not permitted and may result in removal from the group. Practical Philosophy reserves the right to enforce this policy at its discretion to maintain a safe and respectful environment.\n\n**PRACTICAL PHILOSOPHY CLUB - Philosophy, everywhere. ✨**\n\nWe started in Practical Philosophy back in 2021 and there are now 50+ chapters in 25+ countries, including Canada, Spain, Japan, Mexico and many more! 🗺️\n**\\*\\*\\***\n**Join our [Pickering Whatsapp](https://tally.so/r/WORMLP) 👈**\n**Follow us on [Instagram](https://www.instagram.com/practicalphilosophyclub/) 👈**\n**Our [website](https://www.practicalphilosophy.club/) 👈**","startDate":"2026-10-06T23:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"The Shops at Pickering City Center","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Pickering","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1355 Kingston Road, Pickering, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Practical Philosophy Club - Ontario 🇨🇦","url":"https://www.meetup.com/practical-philosophy-club-ontario/"},"performer":"Practical Philosophy Club - Ontario 🇨🇦"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Free Weekly ESL Conversation Meetup","url":"https://www.meetup.com/better-english-cafe/events/316498166/","description":"Practice and improve your English through conversation at St. Andrew Centre (73 Simcoe St, downtown Toronto), while making new friends!\n\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\n\n**How to Get to the Event:**\nBy TTC, exit at St. Andrew Station.\nWalk west on King St. West, passing the church building, to Simcoe St.\nDo not enter through the church building; the large church front doors will be closed.\nAt the corner of Simcoe St. and King St. West, turn and walk south on Simcoe St, looking over Roy Thomson Hall.\nEnter through **St. Andrew Centre**, behind the church building.","startDate":"2026-10-06T23:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-3-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"St. Andrew's Church","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"73 Simcoe St, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Better English Cafe","url":"https://www.meetup.com/better-english-cafe/"},"performer":"Better English Cafe"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Are you Smarter than a Scottish Guy Trivia - One Eyed Jack's Richmond Street","url":"https://www.meetup.com/beer-171/events/316786471/","description":"Our favourite trivia host, Simon from Are You Smarter than a Scottish Guy, is at One-Eyed Jack's (287 Richmond Road - between Spadina and Peter Streets). The beer selection is starting to improve, with several KLB selections; their food menu is very good [https://www.oneeyedjackpub.com/torontomenu](https://www.oneeyedjackpub.com/torontomenu). They have a set of Trivia Night specials, including wings with lots of flavours.\n\nThe trivia starts at 7:00pm with first question around 7:15 pm. We have a set of pair of tables reserved under Steve. Serious RSVPs only as no-shows prevent us from fielding a complete team.\n\nTop prizes is a gift certificate for the next visit. Other prizes are a free round for the table and nachos. There is also a small prize for best team name, so put on your creative hat; the host seems to like puns and prefers short team names.\n\nLet's have some fun, eat some wings, and hopefully win!","startDate":"2026-10-06T22:45:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"One Eyed Jack Restaurant and Bar Toronto","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"287 Richmond St W, Toronto, ON M5V 1X1, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Beer Lovers","url":"https://www.meetup.com/beer-171/"},"performer":"Toronto Beer Lovers"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Free ESL Practice and Support","url":"https://www.meetup.com/meetup-group-mbglenao/events/316580842/","description":"The Church of St. Timothy is excited to offer support to newcomers in Canada. Our goal is to provide conversational language practice through informal instruction and feedback in a welcoming and diverse community. All levels welcome!\n\nWe invite all new-comers, English language students, visitors to Canada, parents of children temporarily attending schools in Toronto, international university students, and anyone looking to enhance their language skills.\nWe aim to build community where friendships can flourish, in order to help participants establish meaningful connections, learn about life in Toronto, and access practical resources as you settle in to this new city and country.\n\nWe begin every Tuesday at 10:00 a.m. with time to socialize. Our formal program begins at 10:30 a.m.\nEach week we will have different activities and topics, including practicing English conversation, reading short articles, learning about common pronunciation and grammar mistakes, etc.\nOur volunteers would love to get to know you and offer gentle and constructive feedback to help you improve your English!","startDate":"2026-10-06T14:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"100 Old Orchard Grove","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"100 Old Orchard Grove, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Church of St. Timothy, North Toronto Meetup Group","url":"https://www.meetup.com/meetup-group-mbglenao/"},"performer":"Church of St. Timothy, North Toronto Meetup Group"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"🎱 learn to play pool 🎱 FREE for ladies 🎱make new friends (Junction) 🎱","url":"https://www.meetup.com/torontobilliardsclub/events/316672256/","description":"🎱**TBC Tuesday Socials at Shoxs**🎉\n\nEnjoy a night of getting out of the house, meeting new people, and enjoying a relaxed night of pool with **Toronto Billiards Club** at **Shoxs**.\n\nThis Tuesday evening social is all about **good vibes, community, and accessible pool**. Whether you are brand new to the game or have years of experience, you will feel comfortable here.\n\n**What to expect:**\n✅ friendly, inclusive, and welcoming social atmosphere\n✅ beginners welcome\n✅ instruction and guidance from TBC hosts\n✅ casual pool games, conversation, drinks, and food\n✅ no pressure, no leagues, no egos\n\nif you have ever thought *“I want to play pool but don’t know where to start”* or *“I don’t want to walk into a pool hall by myself”* this event is made for you. many of our regulars first showed up solo.\n\n💬 **First time attending?**\nOur hosts will introduce you, help you get a game going, and make sure you are comfortable throughout the night.\n\n💵 **Event Fee:**\n$20 per person\n**Payable by cash or e-transfer (dean@tbcpool.org)**\nPlease contact the event organizer if you have payment questions\n\n📋 **House Rules:**\nAll attendees are expected to follow TBC Meetup Rules during the event. If you have questions about rules, fees, or the format, feel free to message an organizer.\n\n👉 **Call to action:**\nBring a friend or come solo. show up curious. Leave with new connections and more confidence at the table.\n\nSee you Tuesday and welcome to the TBC community!\n\n**TBC Admin**","startDate":"2026-10-06T23:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Shoxs","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"2827 Dundas St. W., Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Billiards Club 🎱","url":"https://www.meetup.com/torontobilliardsclub/"},"performer":"Toronto Billiards Club 🎱"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Walk and Salmon watching (hopefully)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/tamclub/events/316460745/","description":"Salmons are expected to be swimming upstream. An annual upward migration. We will spend some time to watch at a few spots and then continue with our walk and return back to the starting point. If you arrive late, pls follow the Humber River Trail heading north and you can catch up with the group.\n\nDistance: 7 to 9km\n\nDifficulty: Very Easy\n\nTrail: Flat Paved Trail\n\n**Transport**\nRecommend taking TTC or Uber.\n\n**TTC**: Get off Old Mill station and walk to the park.\n\n**Parking**: There is Paid & Free Parking available nearby meeting spot. Pls look up if you are driving.\n\n💬 **Stay Connected:**\n***Join Whatsapp Group - [CLICK HERE](https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSflzD3fDrU5sLARAT5yDF3OhEu3Vj-2P7ci8mP5FYX46rt1NQ/viewform)***\n***Follow on Instagram - [CLICK HERE](https://www.instagram.com/tam.club/)***","startDate":"2026-10-06T22:15:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Etienne Brule Park","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"13 Crosby Ave, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Asian Meetup - TAM","url":"https://www.meetup.com/tamclub/"},"performer":"Toronto Asian Meetup - TAM"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Tantric Family Constellation: Temple of Love & Money","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-tantra-circle/events/316588148/","description":"**TANTRIC FAMILY CONSTELLATIONS**\n**Tantric Temple Mysteries**\n\n**This is the project overview only.**\n**Themes and dates may change.**\n\n**To find the exact topic, date and register, please join:**\n\n**t.me/TorontoTantra**\n**t.me/AndyTherapist**\n\n**⸻**\n\n**About this event**\n\n**Tantric Family Constellations is a group practice combining Archetypal / Family Constellations with a living tantric Temple space.**\n\n**Each meeting has its own theme.**\n\n**For example:**\n\n**Love & Money • Ancient Languages of Love • Love & Loneliness • Masculine & Feminine • Desire & Freedom • Relationship Patterns**\n\n**The theme gives us a field to explore — but every participant discovers their own personal story inside it.**\n\n**⸻**\n\n**Part 1 — Discover your pattern**\n\n**We begin by exploring different dimensions of the evening’s theme together.**\n\n**Then each participant goes through a mini-constellation to see their own pattern, model or hidden dynamic.**\n\n**Instead of only thinking about the question, you can see how its different forces are arranged for you:**\n\n**What attracts you?**\n**What do you avoid?**\n**Where does your energy stop?**\n**What are you moving toward?**\n\n**This creates a personal map for the second part of the evening.**\n\n**⸻**\n\n**Part 2 — Enter the Temple**\n\n**Then we open the Tantric Temple.**\n\n**The constellation points become living centers in the space.**\n\n**Participants are free to move between them, following their own inner process.**\n\n**You may stay with one energy, move toward another, step away, return, observe what happens in your body, or allow yourself to gradually absorb a quality that previously felt distant.**\n\n**At the same time, you encounter other participants moving through their own paths.**\n\n**Through presence, movement and consensual interaction, the personal constellation becomes a living group field.**\n\n**There is no fixed choreography and no need to perform.**\n\n**You follow your own rhythm.**\n\n**The practice is about allowing yourself to experience, embody and integrate the different energies of the constellation rather than only understand them intellectually.**\n\n**⸻**\n\n**Why “Temple”?**\n\n**The Temple is a temporary tantric space where symbolic and archetypal energies can be experienced through the body, movement and connection with others.**\n\n**The journey is individual, but it happens inside a shared field.**\n\n**You may discover that a quality which looked abstract during the constellation becomes much more understandable once you can actually move toward it, stay with it and experience it in contact with others.**\n\n**⸻**\n\n**No previous constellation or tantra experience is required.**\n\n**Participation is voluntary, and you can always choose your own level of involvement and contact.**\n\n**The space is based on:**\n\n**consent • respect • confidentiality • personal boundaries • freedom of movement**\n\n**This is a transpersonal personal-growth practice, not a sexual event.**\n\n**Details, themes, dates and registration:**\n**t.me/TorontoTantra**\n\n**Вот более естественный и аккуратный английский вариант, сохраняя твой простой стиль:**\n\n**TICKETS**\n\n1. **Regular Ticket — $100 CAD**\n1. **Early Bird Ticket — $65 CAD**\n**If you register and pay before August 31.**\n**3. Supportive Ticket — $55 CAD**\n**For people with limited financial resources.**\n**4. Bring a Friend — $150 CAD for 2 people**\n\n**If the price is too much for you, send a personal message on Telegram: t.me/AndyTherapist to ask about volunteer options.**\n\n**HOW TO PAY**\n\n**Send an Interac e-Transfer to:**\n**andy.litvinov@gmail.com**\n**After payment, send a screenshot of the confirmation to: t.me/AndyTherapist**\n**Please mention which event you are registering for.**\n\n**After registration, you will be added to the participants’ group.**\n\n**If you have any questions, feel free to message:**\n**t.me/AndyTherapist**\n**Toronto Tantra community:**\n**t.me/TorontoTantra**","startDate":"2026-10-06T23:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"","addressRegion":"","addressCountry":""}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"T.me/TorontoTantra Circle","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-tantra-circle/"},"performer":"T.me/TorontoTantra Circle"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"MASSAGE CLUB & BODY PSYCHOTHERAPY","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-tantra-circle/events/316586675/","description":"MASSAGE CLUB & BODY PSYCHOTHERAPY\nThis is the project overview only!\nDates might change.\n\nTo find the exact dates and register for the event, please join our Telegram group:\n\nT.me/TorontoTantra\nT.me/AndyTherapist\n\nMASSAGE & BODY PSYCHOTHERAPY CLUB\n\nHave you ever explored massage not only as relaxation, but also as a way to reconnect with your body, emotions, and nervous system?\n\nIn Toronto there are many massage services, but not many spaces where people can safely learn, practice and exchange conscious touch together.\n\nWe would like to create such a club.\n\nA warm, respectful space for people interested in massage, bodywork, somatic practices and body-oriented psychotherapy.\n\nYou don’t need professional massage experience. Beginners are welcome.\n\nJoin our group and leave a message if you would like to be added to the waiting list.\nt.me/TorontoTantra\n\nAbout this event\n\n• What is the Massage & Body Psychotherapy Club?\n\nIt is a practice evening where we explore conscious touch, relaxation, massage techniques and simple body-oriented therapeutic exercises.\n\nThe purpose is not only to relax muscles, but also to develop better contact with your body, reduce stress and learn how safe touch can support emotional regulation and connection.\n\n• What will we be doing?\n\nDepending on the evening, we may explore:\n\n- simple relaxation massage techniques\n- conscious touch and body awareness\n- grounding and nervous-system regulation\n- breathing and relaxation exercises\n- somatic and body-psychotherapy exercises\n- practicing giving and receiving\n- communication of boundaries and consent\n\nPractices can be done in pairs or small groups and will be guided step by step.\n\n• Massage exchange\n\nOne of the main parts of the club is a structured massage exchange.\n\nYou can experience both sides:\ngiving touch and receiving touch.\n\nThe goal is not to perform a “perfect massage,” but to become more sensitive to another person’s body, learn to listen through your hands, communicate clearly and discover what kind of touch feels supportive.\n\nImportant terms & agreements\n\nConsent first: every exercise and every touch is optional.\n\nRespect boundaries: you can say yes, no, stop, slower, softer or change the practice at any moment.\n\nKeep it therapeutic: this is a bodywork and personal-development space, not a sexual service or dating event.\n\nStay present: no alcohol or recreational drugs during the event.\n\nConfidentiality: personal experiences shared during the practice stay within the group.\n\nThe club may be interesting for people curious about:\n\nmassage • bodywork • somatic therapy • body-oriented psychotherapy • conscious touch • nervous-system regulation • relaxation • tantra-inspired body awareness\n\nDetails, dates and registration:\nt.me/TorontoTantra","startDate":"2026-10-06T21:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"","addressRegion":"","addressCountry":""}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"T.me/TorontoTantra Circle","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-tantra-circle/"},"performer":"T.me/TorontoTantra Circle"}]</script><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/c/f/7/0/highres_536153104.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head